Chapter: Mbus

 M-Bus (Meter-Bus, EN 13757), the field bus for reading utility meters --
 gas, water, electricity, and heat. Telegrams come in three shapes: a
 single-character acknowledgement (0xE5), a short frame (a fixed
 control/address request), and a long frame carrying a control-
 information field and data. Frames are delimited by a start and a stop
 (0x16) byte and protected by an 8-bit sum checksum over the control,
 address, control-information, and data fields.

Section: Control Fields

  mbus-c-snd-nke : Integer = #40
  mbus-c-snd-ud : Integer = #53
  mbus-c-req-ud2 : Integer = #5B
  mbus-c-rsp-ud : Integer = #08

  mbus-ci-data-send : Integer = #51
  mbus-ci-selection : Integer = #52

Section: Delimiters

  mbus-start-short : Integer = #10
  mbus-start-long : Integer = #68
  mbus-stop : Integer = #16
  mbus-ack : Integer = #E5

Section: Checksum

  mbus-sum : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mbus-sum (bytes) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc else mbus-sum bytes (i + 1) len (acc + list-at bytes i)

  mbus-checksum : List Integer -> Integer
  mbus-checksum (bytes) = bit-and (mbus-sum bytes 0 (list-length bytes) 0) 255

Section: Frames

  mbus-ack-frame : List Integer
  mbus-ack-frame = [mbus-ack]

  mbus-short-frame : Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  mbus-short-frame (c) (a) =
   [mbus-start-short, c, a, bit-and (c + a) 255, mbus-stop]

 The long frame repeats the length (control, address, control-info, and
 data octets) and the start byte, then the body, its checksum, and the
 stop.

  mbus-long-frame : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  mbus-long-frame (c) (a) (ci) (data) =
   let body = [c, a, ci] & data
   in let len = list-length body
   in [mbus-start-long, len, len, mbus-start-long] & body & [mbus-checksum body, mbus-stop]
